        // Manuel
        addItem(ModItems.GUIDE_BOOK, "Orbitalis Manual");
        add("guide.orbitalis.title", "Orbitalis Manual");
        add("guide.orbitalis.welcome.title", "Welcome");
        add("guide.orbitalis.welcome.text", "Welcome to Orbitalis!\n\nThis manual follows the mod's progression, from the first ores to rockets. The easiest way is to read the chapters in order.\n\nYour first goal is steel. To make it, you need ores, power and an arc foundry.\n\nIf JEI is installed, click an item to see its recipe.\n\nAlmost everything is crafted from components, parts that are only used for that. The first two are the heating element (copper, iron, redstone) and the electric motor (steel, copper, iron, redstone). They are enough for the foundry, the generator and the rolling mill. The rest come later: circuit board, flight processor, display, reinforced glass, LED lamp, insulation blanket, steel grating, photovoltaic cell, battery cell, inertial unit, optical sensor, radio transmitter, heat shield tile and CO2 filter. Their tooltip says what they are for.");
        add("guide.orbitalis.ores.title", "Ores");
        add("guide.orbitalis.ores.text", "Three ores generate in the Overworld.\n\nBauxite is common, between Y 32 and 112. A stone pickaxe is enough. It's where aluminum comes from.\n\nLithium is less common, between Y -32 and 48. Stone pickaxe as well.\n\nTitanium is rare, between Y -64 and 16, and needs an iron pickaxe.\n\nEach ore drops its raw form, which you smelt in a furnace or blast furnace to get an ingot. Fortune increases the drops.\n\nNine ingots of steel, aluminum or titanium make a storage block.");
        add("guide.orbitalis.energy.title", "Energy");
        add("guide.orbitalis.energy.text", "Machines run on power, measured in FE.\n\nThe combustion generator makes it. It's crafted from 5 iron ingots, 2 copper ingots, 1 heating element and 1 redstone.\n\n1. Place the generator.\n2. Put your machines against it, or connect them with cables (see \"Cables and Pipes\").\n3. Put fuel in the red slot: coal, wood, a lava bucket...\n\nIt makes 20 FE per tick, and one coal gives 32,000.\n\nThe green gauge on the right shows its 20,000 FE buffer. When it's full, the generator stops burning, so nothing is wasted.\n\nThe small screen shows its state: \"Generating\", \"Buffer full\" or \"No fuel\".");
        add("guide.orbitalis.arc_foundry.title", "Arc Foundry");
        add("guide.orbitalis.arc_foundry.text", "The arc foundry melts two ingredients into an alloy.\n\nIt's crafted from 4 iron ingots, 3 copper ingots, 1 heating element and 1 redstone.\n\nPlace it against a generator and put the ingredients in the two blue slots, in any order. The result comes out in the orange slot.\n\nRecipes:\n- 1 iron ingot + 1 coal = 1 steel ingot (10 s, 6,000 FE)\n- 4 aluminum ingots + 1 lithium ingot = 5 aluminum-lithium ingots (15 s, 15,000 FE)\n\nIf it says \"Not enough energy\", refuel the generator. \"Output full\" means the orange slot needs emptying.");
        add("guide.orbitalis.rolling_mill.title", "Rolling Mill");
        add("guide.orbitalis.rolling_mill.text", "The rolling mill flattens ingots into plates. Plates are what rocket structures and tanks are made of.\n\nIt's crafted from 4 steel ingots, 2 iron ingots, 1 electric motor and 1 redstone.\n\nPut an ingot in the blue slot, and a plate comes out 5 seconds later.\n\nIt makes steel, aluminum, titanium and aluminum-lithium plates. Each costs 2,000 FE, except titanium, which is harder and needs 4,000.");
        add("guide.orbitalis.automation.title", "Automation");
        add("guide.orbitalis.automation.text", "Machines accept hoppers and pipes from other mods.\n\nA hopper pointing into a machine inserts whatever the machine accepts: recipe ingredients, or fuel for the generator.\n\nA hopper underneath only takes what's in the output.\n\nSo a chest of coal hooked to the generator with a hopper keeps it running.\n\nPower uses the FE standard, so cables and generators from other mods work too.");

