        add("guide.orbitalis.research.title", "Research");
        add("guide.orbitalis.research.text", "The skill tree holds all of your agency's research. Open it anywhere with K, which you can change in the game options, under \"Orbitalis: piloting\".\n\nThe Technologies tab has nine rows, one per field: propulsion, structures, avionics, ground infrastructure, satellites, crewed flight, stations, exploration and advanced propulsion. You progress from left to right. A green box is unlocked, a blue one can be researched, a dark one is still waiting on a prerequisite. Drag the view to move around.\n\nClick a box to show its sheet on the right. It lists the cost, what it brings, its prerequisites (sometimes from another field) and the studies it opens at the engineer's workbench. The \"Research\" button, or a double click on the box, spends the points.\n\nResearch points are earned by playing. First steel ingot, first flight, first satellite, first steps on the Moon... The Objectives tab sorts them into six tiers and shows the ones you've already reached. Each one pays only once.\n\nIn multiplayer, an agency is a team (the /team command). Its members share their points and technologies. A player with no team has an agency of their own.");

