        add("guide.orbitalis.shipyard.title", "The Shipyard");
        add("guide.orbitalis.shipyard.text", "No rocket could launch an interstellar ship. So it's built in orbit, at the shipyard attached to the station.\n\nYou need the \"Orbital Shipyard\" technology, which comes after the lunar gateway and fusion propulsion, and the shipyard module, brought on board.\n\nFrom inside the station, right-click a wall with the module. It opens a glazed control room and, behind it, a cradle of beams 31 blocks long, open to space. It needs 13 blocks of width and height.\n\nThe console, facing the window, holds the ship's blueprint, a hull 29 blocks long with a ring 11 blocks across. Missing blocks show as ghosts, and the current section in detail. Place them by hand, or from the console screen with \"Build section\" and \"Build all\", which take the blocks from your inventory.\n\nEach section is built, then fitted out. The warp core goes in the engine room (you need the warp drive), the ring motor on the ceiling, then four hibernation pods, eight grow trays under their lights, and the helm between two consoles. The pods and the core are two blocks tall but placed as a single item.\n\nTo finish, load the core with eight exotic matter with a right-click, then run the check at the helm. It tells you, system by system, what's still missing.");
