        add("fluid.orbitalis.helium_3", "Helium-3");
        add("research.orbitalis.node.helium3", "Lunar Helium-3");
        add("research.orbitalis.node.helium3.desc", "Bake the Moon's regolith to free the solar wind's helium-3, the fuel of fusion. Unlocks the helium-3 extractor.");
        add("guide.orbitalis.helium3.title", "Helium-3");
        add("guide.orbitalis.helium3.text", "Helium-3 is a rare isotope of helium. The solar wind has been depositing it for billions of years in the Moon's regolith, which nothing shields. On the planet, the atmosphere and magnetic field stop it. It's the ideal fuel for fusion, because it gives off almost no neutrons.\n\nIt needs the \"Lunar Helium-3\" technology, which comes after planetary bases.\n\nThe helium-3 extractor is a rotary kiln that heats regolith to around 700 °C. Feed it lunar regolith or, better still, ilmenite ore (mined with Silk Touch), which holds four times more gas. A block of regolith gives 10 mB of helium-3 and 50 mB of hydrogen, and an ilmenite ore 40 mB of helium-3. Helium-3 comes out on the left, hydrogen on the right.\n\nThe machine works anywhere, on the Moon as on the planet, as long as you bring it regolith. It takes a lot, so store helium-3 in a tank for fusion propulsion.");
        add("item.orbitalis.fusion_engine", "Fusion Drive");
        add("block.orbitalis.rocket_engine_fusion", "Fusion Drive (block)");
        add("rocket.orbitalis.propellant.fusion", "D-³He fusion, hydrogen exhaust");
        add("spaceport.orbitalis.fuel_port.he3", "helium-3");
        add("spaceport.orbitalis.pad.helium3", "Helium-3");
        add("creative.orbitalis.rocket.fusion", "Fusion Launcher (test)");
        add("guide.orbitalis.fusion.title", "Fusion");
        add("guide.orbitalis.fusion.text", "Fusion propulsion is the best there is short of speculative technology. A plasma of deuterium and helium-3, held by magnets, heats hydrogen far more than a nuclear engine's reactor.\n\nYou need the \"Fusion Propulsion\" technology, which requires nuclear thermal propulsion and lunar helium-3, then the fusion engine, liquid hydrogen in hydrogen tanks, and helium-3 (see \"Helium-3\").\n\nThe engine has 2,500 s of specific impulse, almost three times the nuclear engine, and 900 kN of vacuum thrust, enough for a crew. It weighs 20 t and never lights on the first stage.\n\nAt the pad, on top of the hydrogen, it needs 1 mB of helium-3 per 20 mB of hydrogen, supplied by a helium-3 fuel port in the back left corner at the foot of the tower.\n\nWith a fusion stage, the Europa ship can go beyond Mercury on a lighter launcher than the nuclear one. For example, four staged-combustion engines and twenty-four composite tanks, a cryogenic engine and twelve composite tanks, then the fusion engine and sixteen hydrogen tanks.");
        add("block.orbitalis.fusion_reactor", "Fusion Reactor");
        add("block.orbitalis.casimir_chamber", "Casimir Chamber");
        add("item.orbitalis.exotic_matter", "Exotic Matter");
        add("propulsion.orbitalis.fusion_reactor.burning", "The plasma is burning: %s FE/t. Helium-3: %s mB, hydrogen: %s mB. Stored: %s kFE.");
        add("propulsion.orbitalis.fusion_reactor.no_fuel", "Off: it needs helium-3 and hydrogen gas, by pipe. Helium-3: %2$s mB, hydrogen: %3$s mB.");
        add("propulsion.orbitalis.fusion_reactor.full", "Standing by: its store is full (%4$s kFE). Connect cables or machines to it.");
        add("guide.orbitalis.fusion_power.title", "The Fusion Reactor");
        add("guide.orbitalis.fusion_power.text", "The fusion reactor holds a plasma of deuterium and helium-3 in a ring of magnets. It's the biggest power source in the mod, 1,200 FE per tick, thirty times what a machine uses.\n\nIt needs the \"Fusion Propulsion\" technology.\n\nPipe helium-3 and gaseous hydrogen into it, on any face (hydrogen from the electrolyzer, not liquid hydrogen). It burns 2 mB of helium-3 and 20 mB of hydrogen every second, and sends its power to the cables and machines touching it. It stores up to 1,000,000 FE and shuts down when full. Right-click it to see its status.\n\nThe Casimir chamber makes exotic matter. Between two mirrors almost touching, the vacuum itself digs out negative energy. Put an ender pearl in it, and a minute and 480,000 FE later it comes out as exotic matter, the key to the warp drive.\n\nA single reactor is enough to run three Casimir chambers.");
        add("design.orbitalis.no_payload", "No payload");
